Live metadata transfer can race in-flight writes
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/a598d0273ea881919344a677f03c9628?sev=&repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin
Criticality: medium (attack path: medium)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit [`efec86dd`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/efec86ddda12d27f63270d764a193f5d8855a6ef) (`Drain source leases before live metadata transfer export`).

The finding was valid for the reported commit `918c9cb`: the live metadata-transfer command fenced the source PG and immediately exported/imported metadata without waiting for previously issued Active route leases to expire. A stale frontend or storage-node view could therefore still commit a metadata command on the old source after the export snapshot had been taken.

The fix makes the live transfer fence return and persist the source active primary lease deadline. The admin command now waits for that deadline before exporting, refreshes the fenced Peering runtime map after the wait, and verifies the source route still matches the fenced source node. Retry/interruption handling is also fail-closed: already-fenced PGs reuse the persisted deadline, and older fenced records without a stored deadline wait conservatively for the maximum unexpired source acting-set lease instead of guessing from the first acting-set member.

Regression coverage includes the exact retry fallback case `fenced_metadata_transfer_retry_without_stored_deadline_uses_max_source_lease`, the live-command wait helper test `metadata_transfer_source_lease_wait_duration_waits_until_deadline`, and the existing metadata-transfer/control-plane suites. Verification for the resolution:
- `cargo test -p storage fenced_metadata_transfer_retry_without_stored_deadline_uses_max_source_lease -- --nocapture`
- `cargo test -p storage metadata_transfer -- --nocapture`
- `cargo test -p storage control_plane -- --nocapture`
- `cargo test -p argmin-s3 metadata_transfer -- --nocapture`
- `./scripts/uat-s3-tests --smoke metadata-pg-migration`
- `cargo nextest run` passed 5590 tests.

